    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110859" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλάνωρ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾱ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, 
			Dor.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλήνωρ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fond of a man, amorous,
				conjugal,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στίβοι, τρόποι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				411
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				856
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					136
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.):—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλήνωρ</span></b>  only in late 
				Ep.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Musae.
				267
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Coluth.
				213
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>kindly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξείνων φ. τιμά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					1.40
				</span></i>
			; <i>fond of men,</i> of dolphins, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιοτά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					236
				</span></i>
			.</div>
